; A `(pass …)` with a `post()` that samples its input without reading `pngine`.
;
; This did not compile before §393's second half. The pass sugar numbers each
; pipeline's prelude from 0 INDEPENDENTLY, so:
;
;   main shader: pngine at 0, samp at 1 (declared for post(), unused by fs()),
;                postTex at 2 — its group binds only the uniform at 0
;   post shader: no uniform, so samp at 0 and postTex at 1 — its group binds both
;
; Both are internally consistent. The bind-kind check joined them through a
; document-wide (group, binding) key with no pipeline in it, read (0,1) as "a
; texture" from the post group, and compared it against `samp` reflected out of
; the MAIN shader:
;
;   binding 'samp' (@group(0) @binding(1)) is bound as a texture in SJON
;   but the shader declares a sampler
;
; Nothing in this document is wrong; the join was. Adding `pngine.width` to
; post() used to make it compile, which is the tell — the trigger was the post
; shader's numbering shifting down by one.
(pass-graph
  (pass :name main :code """
    @fragment fn fs(@builtin(position) pos: vec4f) -> @location(0) vec4f {
      let uv = pos.xy / vec2f(pngine.width, pngine.height);
      return vec4f(uv, sin(pngine.time) * .5 + .5, 1);
    }

    @fragment fn post(@builtin(position) pos: vec4f) -> @location(0) vec4f {
      let uv = pos.xy / vec2f(512., 512.);
      let c = textureSample(postTex, samp, uv);
      return vec4f(c.rgb * 1.2, 1);
    }
  """))
